        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "34619fad-9da0-5e14-bdce-13337f09dc2a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean Dubuffet\n- Organizations: NME\n- Bands: Art Brut, Franz Ferdinand, The Rakes, Bloc Party\n- Places: South London, Glasgow\n- Concepts: outsider art, Art Wave\n- Albums: You Could Have It So Much Better\n\nFacts:\n- Jean Dubuffet defined outsider art as art made by prisoners, loners, mentally ill people, and other marginalized people without concern for imitation or presentation.\n- Franz Ferdinand are a Scottish rock band that formed in 2002 and are based in Glasgow.\n- South London's Art Brut took their name from Jean Dubuffet's term Art Brut.\n- NME tagged Art Brut as part of the Art Wave scene alongside bands including The Rakes, Franz Ferdinand, and Bloc Party.\n- You Could Have It So Much Better is the second studio album by the Scottish indie rock band Franz Ferdinand.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
